
HOW TO USE THE ROUTINES AND GRIDS TO EXTRACT THE AKK FFS

All the FORTRAN routines that you need are in "akk.f". Put this file
and all grids in the same directory as your main program. Write
"include 'akk.f'" at the bottom of your main program. The extraction
is done by issuing in your main program the command "CALL
AKK(IH,Z,Q,DH)". For these arguments' meanings, see the comments in
"SUBROUTINE AKK(IH,Z,Q,DH)", at the top of "akk.f".

The file "ffakk.f" contains an example main program for extracting the
AKK FFs. It is sufficient to compile ffakk.f (and hence the akk.f
routines) with the command

g77 -o ffakk ffakk.f

or something similar for a different compiler.

The values of LambdaQCD for 3, 4 and 5 flavours are returned in the
array lambdaQCD(3:5) by "CALL AKK_LAMBDAQCD(LAMBDAQCD)" (see ffakk.f)

FFs are not provided in the range 0.05 < z, since they were not
determined there.  Furthermore, FFs are only provided in the range 1
GeV < Q < sqrt(100000) GeV --- if you need a larger range, please
contact me. Note that the validity of the fixed order approximation to
DGLAP evolution is dubious in the region Q < O(1) GeV.
